  "goodToKnow": "Der Zwangsarbeiter or die Zwangsarbeiterin is a forced labourer. Nazi Germany deported millions of people, mostly from Eastern Europe, to work in factories, farms and households. In 2000 the state and companies founded the foundation Erinnerung, Verantwortung und Zukunft, which paid compensation to surviving former forced labourers. Der Zwang means compulsion. The plural is the same."
